  "scope": "# Review: ead22faa41ef\n\nTask/source: `ead22faa41ef`, generator `3.1.0`, source SHA-256 `ffcf07292e27f9a5788fe93109327ec123b281d8c35797dfa6f007c33c09dfd9`.\nDefect: a default three-demo lesson could omit all lone 3/2 witnesses, so global color replacement fit every demo and changed the query.\nRepair: declare that rival and use a period-2 default schedule whose witness slots preserve at least one lone 3 and lone 2; every three-of-four rotation now retains a refuting demo.\nCanonical authority: unchanged (`RULE_HASH=6615d26334ba`; Racket SHA-256 `fc2471b9a0fe8f3bf1318728a845cb54408e2d80744b6da6deca664a681cdbaa`).\nProposed prototype: episode-fixed `survivor_role={green3,red2}` under `workspace/parametric/`; `green3` is byte-exact canonical and `red2` swaps the surviving pair role.\nFocused tests: 24 passed plus 14 subtests in `checks/ead22faa41ef-task-tests-after/result.json`.\nTeaching check: 12/12 lessons identifiable and 0/48 ambiguous rotations in `checks/ead22faa41ef-semantic-after-final/`.\nRacket prototype evidence: 4 canonical and 14 episode labels replayed, 2 settings, 8 queries, zero ambiguities in `checks/parametric/survivor-role/report.json`.\nAdversarial pass: 56 independent parity labels passed; public-byte tampering was rejected (`checks/parametric/survivor-role-adversarial.json`).\nStatus: scoped repair and prototype complete; no remaining scoped test failure. Prototype approval/shared integration/training remain explicitly out of scope.",
